  "text": "Thermodynamics! Energy transformations from one form into another under certain conditions. Chemical energy stored by molecules. Methane cooking gas or coal fuel. Fuel burns in air, reactions. Fuel burns in an engine, work mechanical. Galvanic cell like Tricel, energy electrical. Forms of energy interrelated, transform from one form into another form. Thermodynamics! Her energy transformations from one form into another based on certain conditions. Vital state! Laws deal with energy changes of a system undergoing the change. Macroscopic, a large number of molecules rather than microscopic, a few molecules. Thermodynamics, study of these transformations. Not how, not at what rate, based on initial state, final state. Laws apply only when a system is in equilibrium or moves state to state equilibrium. Do equilibrium, pressure, temperature in equilibrium, do not change with time. Thermodynamics, study of these transformations, not how, not at what rate, based on initial state, final state.",
